NNOOTTEESS
       pptthhrreeaadd__kkiillll__ootthheerr__tthhrreeaaddss__nnpp() is intended to be called just before a
       thread calls eexxeeccvvee(2) or a similar function.  This function is
       designed to address a limitation in the obsolete LinuxThreads
       implementation whereby the other threads of an application are not
       automatically terminated (as POSIX.1‐2001 requires) during eexxeeccvvee(2).

